  - randomx
  - proof-of-work
  - cover-traffic
abstract: >
  A family of protocols that leverage the inherent randomness of
  cryptocurrency mining traffic to provide resilient communication
  channels. The Stratum mining protocol — used by Bitcoin, Monero, Kaspa,
  and others — provides a high-entropy, economically motivated transport
  substrate for data encapsulation. Includes Visual Stratum (data
  encapsulation in Stratum mining shares), Mining Gate (proof-of-work
  gated access control), and Falo (anonymous group coordination via
  zero-knowledge proofs).
notes: "Reference implementation v1.1.0-draft02 — implements VS3 protocol (v3.0.0). See repository for full protocol version history."
